---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const cv = `${base}cv/`;
const email = 'mailto:c.fernandez@geosmart.es';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — GeoSmart" description="Get to know Camila Fernández — geology undergraduate building a path towards petroleum-focused subsurface and offshore geoscience.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-kicker">The geologist behind GeoSmart</div>
      <h1>Curious about<br />what lies beneath.</h1>
      <p class="muted">A geology student building a path towards petroleum-focused subsurface and offshore geoscience.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page">
    <div class="container profile">
      <div class="profile-photo">
        <span>Your field photo<br />goes here.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="section-kicker">Hi, I'm Camila.</p>
        <h2>I like geology because it is part science, part detective work.</h2>
        <p>I'm a geology undergraduate at the Universidad Complutense de Madrid, currently continuing my training at NTNU in Trondheim. I'm particularly interested in the subsurface: how geological history, physical properties and geophysical data come together to help us understand what we cannot see directly.</p>
        <p>My interests sit at the intersection of <strong>subsurface geology, geophysics, sedimentology and energy resources</strong>, with a growing focus on seismic interpretation, petrophysics and geological reservoirs.</p>

        <h2>What I'm building</h2>
        <div class="focus-grid">
          <article class="focus-card"><div class="card-tag">01 / Subsurface</div><h3>Petroleum geology</h3><p>Geological reasoning below the surface and in energy-related settings.</p></article>
          <article class="focus-card"><div class="card-tag">02 / Geophysics</div><h3>Seismic interpretation</h3><p>Using geophysical evidence to understand structures and the subsurface.</p></article>
          <article class="focus-card"><div class="card-tag">03 / Sediments</div><h3>Reservoir thinking</h3><p>Depositional environments, sedimentary records and geological reservoirs.</p></article>
          <article class="focus-card"><div class="card-tag">04 / Mapping</div><h3>GIS &amp; field geology</h3><p>Turning spatial data and observations into useful geological information.</p></article>
        </div>

        <h2>Where I'm heading</h2>
        <p>I'm building towards a career in <strong>petroleum-focused offshore and North Sea geoscience</strong>, especially exploration and subsurface work. At NTNU, I'm expanding my Bachelor's training through petroleum-focused geoscience coursework and subjects that complement what is available in my degree in Spain.</p>
        <p>I want to keep developing the technical skills needed to interpret geological and geophysical data while understanding the bigger geological story behind them. For me, good geoscience is not only about getting an interpretation right. It's also about being able to explain <em>why</em> it makes sense.</p>

        <h2>More than geology</h2>
        <p>My background also includes <strong>project coordination, technical documentation, client and cross-team communication, international business support</strong> and digital operations. I enjoy working where technical knowledge has to become clear, organised and useful to other people.</p>
        <p>Through science outreach and <strong>@_geomila_</strong>, I also share geology in a way that feels curious, visual and approachable. GeoSmart brings those two sides together: the technical work I'm learning to do and the stories that make geology worth looking at in the first place.</p>

        <h2>A little more about my path</h2>
        <div class="timeline-mini">
          <p><strong>Universidad Complutense de Madrid</strong><br /><span>BSc in Geology · 2021–present</span></p>
          <p><strong>NTNU, Trondheim</strong><br /><span>Petroleum-focused geoscience coursework · 2026–27</span></p>
        </div>

        <div class="contact-box">
          <div class="section-kicker">Like what you see?</div>
          <h2>Want to know more?</h2>
          <p>This page is the short version. For the full picture — experience, education, certifications, skills and everything in between — have a look at my CV.</p>
          <div class="about-links">
            <a class="btn" href={cv}>Download my CV →</a>
            <a class="text-link dark" href={email}>Let's talk →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
